### v1.0.68 -- `status.ts` DID NOT EXIST

At v1.0.68, the file `packages/opencode/src/session/status.ts` did not exist. Session status tracking was not yet a separate module. The session module (`session/index.ts`) used `SessionLock` (via `lock.ts`) for busy/idle tracking, and there was no `session.idle` or `session.status` bus event.

---

## The `Info` type -- all possible `status.type` values

There are exactly **3 status types**, and they have been the same since `status.ts` was first created:

| `type` | Additional fields | Semantics |
|--------|------------------|-----------|
| `"idle"` | (none) | Session is not actively processing. This is the default state -- if a session has no entry in the status map, it is considered `idle`. When set to idle, the session is removed from the in-memory status map. Also triggers the deprecated `session.idle` event. |
| `"busy"` | (none) | Session is actively processing a request (the agent loop is running). |
| `"retry"` | `attempt: number`, `message: string`, `next: number` | Session hit a retryable error (e.g., rate limit) and is waiting to retry. `attempt` is the retry attempt number, `message` is the error description, `next` is the timestamp (ms since epoch) of the next retry. |

**There are no comments in the source explaining the semantics of each type.** The behavior is inferred from the code:
- When `set()` is called with `idle`, the session is **deleted** from the status map (so absent = idle).
